  <widget type="textupdate" version="2.0.0">
    <name>InterlockWR</name>
    <pv_name>$(P):ILK:TIME_WR_S</pv_name>
    <x>215</x>
    <y>145</y>
    <width>330</width>
    <height>28</height>
    <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    <tooltip>$(P):ILK:TIME_WR_S (TIME_WR_S_ILK)

White Rabbit timestamp latched by the FPGA at the moment the interlock fired,
formatted as YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.nnnnnnnnn. This is the time to use when
correlating the event with the rest of the accelerator.</tooltip>
  </widget>
  <widget type="textupdate" version="2.0.0">
    <name>InterlockSYS</name>
    <pv_name>$(P):ILK:TIME_SYS_S</pv_name>
    <x>560</x>
    <y>145</y>
    <width>325</width>
    <height>28</height>
    <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    <tooltip>$(P):ILK:TIME_SYS_S (TIME_SYS_S_ILK)

System clock timestamp at which the IOC detected the interlock edge. The
difference to the White Rabbit event time is the detection latency of the
IOC.</tooltip>
  </widget>
  <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
    <name>InterlockWRLabel</name>
    <text>White Rabbit event time</text>
    <x>215</x>
    <y>173</y>
